// c-cost-misc-06: the node-walk keeps about 21 KB per activation. Every call
// is a retained activation by design; this measures what one costs. f's
// body is about 22 nodes; f(6, x) is 127 activations, so 1000 slots make
// 127000 of them.
//
// command (from the repo root; read the peak RSS, e.g. VmHWM):
//   GRAPHIX_PAR=off graphix --no-cache --no-fusion design/review-2026-10-05/repro/c-cost-misc-06.gx
// vary the depth (6 below) to get the slope.
//
// expected: a footprint per activation in proportion to a 22-node body.
//
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): peak RSS by depth (activations per
// slot): 0 (1): 106 MB; 1 (3): 147 MB; 3 (15): 409 MB; 4 (31): 754 MB;
// 6 (127): 2790 MB. That is 20.4-21.6 KB per activation, and it stays: at
// depth 4 VmRSS holds 752 MB after the cycle, idle. Fused (no --no-fusion)
// depth 6 peaks at 69 MB. A plain array::map(array::init(n, |i| i), |x| x *
// 2 + 1) with its fold costs about 25 KB a slot node-walked (582 MB at
// 21000 slots, 82 MB at 1000). A 20000-slot map at depth 6 extrapolates to
// about 53 GB.
let rec f = |d: i64, v: i64| -> i64 select d { 0 => v, d => (f(d - 1, v + 1) + f(d - 1, v * 3)) % 1000003 };
let ys = array::map(array::init(1000, |i| i), |x| f(6, x));
let r = array::fold(ys, 0, |a, b| (a + b) % 1000003);
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:50.ms, r ~ 0));
r
